{title: Before the Rooster Crows}
{subtitle: Matthew 26:69–75; 26:33–35; Luke 22:54–62}
{key: Bbm}
{tempo: 66}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bbm] | [Bbm] | [Bbm] | [Bbm] |
| [Bbm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I told him even if they all fall away, Lord, I never will
Even if I must [Eb]die with you, I'd be standing with you still
He looked at me and told [Bbm]me what this very night would bring
Before the rooster crows, you will deny me three times
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
They led him to the high priest's house, I followed far behind
[Eb]They kindled a fire in the courtyard and I sat down [Bbm]in the light
A servant girl looked close at me and said this man was with him too
I said woman, I don't know him, and I didn't know what to do
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Before the rooster crows
Before the rooster crows
You will deny me three times
And he went [Eb]outside and wept bitterly
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
A lit[Bbm]tle later someone said, you are one of them too
I said man, I am not, I don't know what you're talking to
[Ebm]An hour later, your accent gives you away, they [Bbm]swore
[Ebm]And I began to curse and swear, I do not know the man, no [Bbm]more
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Before the rooster crows [Ebm][Bbm]
Before the rooster crows
You will deny me three times
And he went outside and wept bitterly
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
At that very moment, while [Ebm]he was still speaking, the rooster crowed
The Lord turned and looked [Bbm]straight at Peter
And Peter remembered the [Ebm]word the Lord had spoken
Three times I said I ne[Bbm]ver knew him
The one who knew [Ebm]me best of all
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
He went outside and wept bit[Bbm]terly
Before the rooster crows
{end_of_verse}
